Prometheus77 <aaronsama@gmail.com> wrote:
> My rogue is coming up on the castle. I haven't gotten a wish yet,
> but did get Stormbringer from sacrificing and have completed the
> quest for the MKoT and the Bell of Opening. I'd like to wish for
> Grayswandir or Magicbane (can't decide which). My question is, do
> I have 2 or 3 artifacts for purposes of calculating my wish success rate?

Only two artifacts; the invocation "artifacts", while unique and often
called "artifacts", are not actually considered artifacts by the game
internally.

A nice way this can be seen is to enter wizard mode and try
to wish for an artifact - say, Magicbane - twice; the second attempt
will only result in an ordinary athame. Wishing twice for an invocation
item will make the game complain that you already have the [item] (it's
supposed to be unique, after all):
  already have silver bell?
  Program in disorder - perhaps you'd better #quit.
  p - a Bell of Opening.

For obvious reasons, this is only possible in wizard mode. (In a strange
way, this makes "unique" items possibly less unique than artifacts in
wizard mode.)


